{{!-- The table of contents, in the two shapes the design draws it.

	{{> "post/toc" variant="inline"}}   A1's open disclosure above the article
	{{> "post/toc" variant="rail"}}     A2's list at the top of the sticky rail

THE LIST IS BUILT FROM THE ARTICLE, NOT FROM A FIXTURE. Ghost has no table-of-contents helper
and a template cannot read inside {{content}}, so `postToc` (assets/js/main.js) walks the
rendered headings on boot and this markup is the shape it fills. That is not a workaround for
a missing helper — it is the only construction that stays true when an author adds a section:
there is no second list to update, and a post whose body has no headings renders no block at
all rather than an empty box.

Which headings count is a design decision: h2 only. The design's own contents lists the four
chapter headings and skips the h3 under one of them, and a contents list that mirrors every
level of a long essay stops being navigation.

The numbers are the position in the list, not part of the heading, so they are generated
here. The ids are Ghost's: its renderer slugifies every heading and de-duplicates collisions
with a numeric suffix, so the anchors are the platform's own and survive an export. --}}

{{#match variant "inline"}}
	<details
		open
		x-data="postToc"
		x-show="items.length"
		x-cloak
		class="border-border bg-surface mb-11 rounded-sm border">
		<summary
			class="font-ui text-muted cursor-pointer px-[18px] py-3.5 text-[13px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] uppercase">{{t "On this page"}}</summary>

		<ol class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-2.5 px-[18px] pb-[18px]">
			<template
				x-for="item in items"
				x-bind:key="item.id">
				<li class="flex gap-3">
					<span
						class="text-muted font-mono text-[11px]"
						x-text="item.num"></span>
					<a
						x-bind:href="'#' + item.id"
						x-bind:aria-current="item.id === active ? 'true' : null"
						x-bind:class="item.id === active ? 'text-accent font-semibold' : 'text-muted'"
						class="font-ui text-sm no-underline"
						x-text="item.label"></a>
				</li>
			</template>
		</ol>
	</details>
{{/match}}

{{#match variant "rail"}}
	<nav
		x-data="postToc"
		x-show="items.length"
		x-cloak
		aria-label="{{t "On this page"}}"
		class="border-border border-b pb-5">
		<p class="text-muted mb-3.5 font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "On this page"}}</p>

		<ol class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-[11px] p-0">
			<template
				x-for="item in items"
				x-bind:key="item.id">
				<li class="flex gap-2.5">
					<span
						class="text-muted font-mono text-[11px]"
						x-text="item.num"></span>
					<a
						x-bind:href="'#' + item.id"
						x-bind:aria-current="item.id === active ? 'true' : null"
						x-bind:class="item.id === active ? 'text-accent font-semibold' : 'text-muted'"
						class="font-ui text-[13.5px] leading-[1.4] no-underline"
						x-text="item.label"></a>
				</li>
			</template>
		</ol>
	</nav>
{{/match}}
